<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sula (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sula is a river of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, about 360 km long, a left tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>. Romny and Lubny stand on its banks. In the 10th and 11th centuries it formed part of the southern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> against the steppe nomads.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sula-river.jpg" alt="Sula (river)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drool_88 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sula_River_in_Ukraine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
